 "text": "Brown County Ohio Government Portal - Auditor\nHome\nFAQs\nLinks\nTowns & Villages\nNews\nBrown County Auditor\nAuditor Jill Hall\nAddress\nCounty Administration Building\nSuite# 181\n800 Mt. Orab Pike\nGeorgetown, Ohio 45121\nTelephone 937.378.6398 or (toll free) 888.244.6420\nFax 937.378.6038\nOffice Hours 7:30 a.m. - 4:00 p.m. Monday-Friday.\nWebsite http://www.BrownCountyAuditor.org\nEmail JHall@BrownCountyAuditor.org\nMost people know the Auditor as the county official who calculates thier property tax bills and reappraiser the value of real property (land and improvements) every six years. As the county's chief fiscal officer, the Auditor also makes sure that expenditures made anywhere in county government follow the law.\nCounty Commissioners depend on the Auditor each year to certify an estimate of total taxes and other revenues that is then made available to the county budget for appropriations to other county officials, agencies and departments.\nElected Officials\nAuditor\nClerk of Courts\nCommissioners\nCommon Pleas\nCoroner\nEngineer\nMunicipal Judge\nProbate/Juvenile\nProsecutor\nRecorder\nSheriff\nTreasurer\nQuick Information\n∙ Brown-Adams County Resource Guide\n∙ County Map\n∙ Brown County Comprehensive Plan\n∙ Legal Holidays\n∙ School Districts\n∙ Telephone Numbers\n∙ Emergency Info\n∙ Township Officials\nNews & Postings\nContractor Information: Community Housing Impact & Preservation Program (CHIP) Contractor\nAberdeen\nFayetteville\nGeorgetown\nHamersville\nHigginsport\nMount Orab\nRipley\nRussellville\nSardinia\nSaint Martin\nLake Lorelei\nLake Waynoka",
